{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1446573-mummies-and-cross-splat-chronicles","id":1446573,"title":"Mummies and cross-splat chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-30T01:50:56-07:00","id":1446573,"title":"Mummies and cross-splat chronicles","content":"I'm currently running a vampire chronicle, but I'm trying to include a bit of everything. Even though it is centered on Vampire: The Requiem, I've given the players the option to make characters from other splats as backups, or for one off scenarios. I'd really like to include Mummy, but I'm not sure how that would work considering Mummies work backwards to every other splat for CoD. It's a low power chronicle (BP 2) so that would mean any Mummy characters would have to be at the tail end of their Descent already. Would that actually work, or is it not possible to mix Mummies with other splats? Was it intentional that Mummy not be compatible with all the other splats for CoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 04-30-2021, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T04:49:25-07:00","id":1446583,"title":"","content":"Would it work? I see why not. <br /> Is it not possible? I don\u2019t see why so. <br /> Intentionally incompatible? Probably nah. <br /> <br /> I admit my grasp of Mummy rules &amp; lore is sketchy, but the trick here seems to be placing good narrative reasons why the early-Descent, high-Sekhem mummy cannot or really, <i>really</i> should not go all-out Old Testament style on everything. I\u2019ll need to do some more reading to tell what that could be, though.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I\u2019m pretty sure there are <i>some</i> ways to keep a late-Descent, low-Sekhem mummy in action long enough for a given story to finish, especially for 2E. (Like how some games/books have a major character retiring/slumbering at the \u201cWhere are they now\u201d epilogue; meaning they played out the entire story afterall)<br /> <br /> If all fails, maybe playing some other \u2018Mummy splat\u2019 like a Sadikh or sorcerer could work. Or an immortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Grammer 04-30-2021, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:20:35-07:00","id":1446625,"title":"","content":"I was able to use a recently arisen mummy once, in a mage game, where the PCs were starting characters. I think they had dropped to Sekhem 6 when the PCs first encountered them. The game didn\u2019t last long enough to fully see how well that was going to work, but while we were playing, no major issues came up.<br /> <br /> The trick to it is being very deliberate about everyones motives and the nature of the conflict between them. Basically, treat a mummy like a spirit, who wakes up at Rank 6 and gradually gets weaker - Plot Device characters. [and, if you want really excellent advice for how to use Plot Device characters, look up Dresden Files RPG - Paranet Papers.] Make sure the PCs know if they try to challenge the Mummy directly, they\u2019ll probably get smote, but give them other weaknesses to exploit (like going after cultists), or ways of going \u201caround\u201d the mummy instead of through them.<br /> When I use them as NPCs, I tend to have everyone regard mummies a bit like natural disasters: stay out of their way, let them do their thing, and soon they\u2019ll go to sleep. That\u2019s a fine attitude for other NPCs, but won\u2019t be satisfying for the PCs - so build in ways they can undermine the mummy\u2019s plan (or redirect it against their enemies) without dying.<br /> <br /> Low Sekhem mummies (1-3), though, can be used more similar to other splats. They won\u2019t be able to boost their attributes (at least no higher than a vampire). They lose access to one or two tiers of Utterance, so their powers are much less overwhelming. At that point, I think vampires (especially a group of them) might even have the advantage in physical conflict. Toward the end of their Descent, mummies have often fulfilled their First Purpose, and are working on personal goals and long term projects - that or they\u2019re Really Desperate to complete their mission; it\u2019s a good point for anyone with a grievance to try settling the score. Carefully - you don\u2019t want the next time they wake up to be for the purpose of \u201ckill that vampire\u201d. But their cults and allies are still potent threat, and their powers can still be pretty powerful - they\u2019ll just probably be relying on Affinities more, which are more subtle.<br /> <br /> I like to use Low Sekhem mummies (or their cults, for a longer term antagonist) to emphasize the role as \u201cshepherds of civilization\u201d, having them engage in politics and long term planning for guild business - setting up huge changes in human culture to play out over the next decade. Particularly in ways that oppose the PCs factions. Mummies are scary because they smite you, but they\u2019re antagonists because they change the layout of Dragon Nests, invest in transformative developments in technology and city planning, inspire religious and non-profit organizations, and find just the lever to shake up (or lock down) the course of politics for a generation. Ie, Stuff that can strip vampires of all their pawns and territories, and may even give the Herd protection against them.<br /> So, you know, I think they\u2019re fantastic to use as a foil to vampires.<br /> In fact, I\u2019m planning a mummy chronicle where vampires will be the main antagonists. Because their political back-and-forth can be so interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:38:05-07:00","id":1446631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1446573-mummies-and-cross-splat-chronicles?p=1446583#post1446583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit my grasp of Mummy rules &amp; lore is sketchy, but the trick here seems to be placing good narrative reasons why the early-Descent, high-Sekhem mummy cannot or really, <i>really</i> should not go all-out Old Testament style on everything. I\u2019ll need to do some more reading to tell what that could be, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their main reason for not unleashing their full power generally seems to be \u201cit tends to undermine their long term plans.\u201d It feels good to rain meteors on your enemies, but you\u2019re likely to destroy relics, ruin a century\u2019s worth of work for all of your allies, piss of the Judges, and send out a flare for all of your enemies. Once there\u2019s a supernatural willing to be that obvious and destructive, you can pretty much get everyone else in the setting to ally against them, scatter their ashes, and wipe out their cult.<br /> <br /> And some of their enemies have really, really scary things they can do to a mummy. Like eat their soul and bind them to eternal slavery to the force of entropy. Or, if the mummy fucks up badly enough themselves, their master shows up to put things back on track through abject cruelty to everything the mummy values, and ensure their next \u201cslumber\u201d is as awful as possible.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d probably recommend Not using a manifested Judge in a non-mummy game, though. That\u2019s... cosmic tier stuff, very much tied to mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T09:21:50-07:00","id":1446802,"title":"","content":"So the thing to remember about Mummies is that they are in principle similar to playing a powerful Primogen elder. They are extremely deadly and usually endowed with incredible occult powers, they have a great deal of influence and plenty of people to serve as minions...but they are prone to taking long naps as the years go by and in general have little to no knowledge of the modern world. Cults are sort of baked into the rules to provide a resource for mummies to get around the simple difficulties of being unable to drive a car, use a smart phone, maybe even speak the current language. What's more, a mummy can't use most of his most outrageous abilities without striking nearby mortals with supernatural terror of his existence. Also, a mummy has to obey the will of his Judge and the direction of his Cult if he wants his Descent to last awhile.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is deprive the mummy of the resources of his cult. Maybe something slaughtered them. Maybe something corrupted them. Furthermore, I would suggest restricting a Mummy's ability to cause massive destruction in some way. Perhaps the spell that brings them back to life is filled with caveats and restrictions that prevent as much as possible the Mummy from directly harming the threat to his cult. So he is cut off from anything that would normally help him navigate the mortal world. Except that vampires thrive in this arena. They are the masters of social interaction and mortal manipulation. They can be strong in situations the mummy is weak, but might have to rely on the Mummy in situation where neonates would normally not stand a chance. I'd suggest a common enemy for them to face, probably whatever is messing with the Mummy's cult. Just give the Mummy a reason to rely on the vampires like he would his cult, and give the players mutual scenarios of advantage and disadvantage to let everyone shine. A mummy will find it difficult to maneuver in social situations a vampire walks through with ease, for example, but a mummy can take on threats normal vampires would find intimidating. Make the challenges broader than the advantages of either super and it should balance itself out. The mummy can be the muscle and the vampires can be the Face, if you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T10:17:46-07:00","id":1450183,"title":"","content":"How long can Mummies hang out at low Sekhem; Long enough for a Chronicle? Will you have timeskips where nothing interesting happens, and a Mummy could die &amp; come back? Can someone contact &amp; bargain with your Judge to simplify your returns, maybe a Cruac ritual for vampires? If you want it to be easier for the Mummy to stay awake, I\u2019d make a McGuffin from another splat (so it can break normal mummy rules) that can maintain Sekhem at a low level. Vampire could be something to convert Vitae, GodMachine some sort of cthonic infrastructure, etc.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d also suggest introducing a mummy character in media res after their Sekhem has dropped to non-overpowered levels. Maybe work with the player to figure out any big events the Mummy caused while at high Sekhem, and work dealing with any aftermath into this chronicle. So they get to feel like they used their high end powers, without disrupting the normal game. Which could mean a death&amp;return later in the chronicle right before confronting someone powerful. Suuuuuper-duck for just long enough to beat down the Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T13:56:07-07:00","id":1450224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1446573-mummies-and-cross-splat-chronicles?p=1450183#post1450183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long can Mummies hang out at low Sekhem; Long enough for a Chronicle? Will you have timeskips where nothing interesting happens, and a Mummy could die &amp; come back? Can someone contact &amp; bargain with your Judge to simplify your returns, maybe a Cruac ritual for vampires? If you want it to be easier for the Mummy to stay awake, I\u2019d make a McGuffin from another splat (so it can break normal mummy rules) that can maintain Sekhem at a low level. Vampire could be something to convert Vitae, GodMachine some sort of cthonic infrastructure, etc.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d also suggest introducing a mummy character in media res after their Sekhem has dropped to non-overpowered levels. Maybe work with the player to figure out any big events the Mummy caused while at high Sekhem, and work dealing with any aftermath into this chronicle. So they get to feel like they used their high end powers, without disrupting the normal game. Which could mean a death&amp;return later in the chronicle right before confronting someone powerful. Suuuuuper-duck for just long enough to beat down the Prince.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are ways to prolong the Descent into duat for certain. If a Mummy is a good boy and does something pleasing to a Judge, like build a monument in honor of Irem or murder someone while declaring loudly they do so in the name of said Judge their current clock &quot;resets&quot; at the base level. For example, a mummy with one remaining Sekhem usually has 2 stories or 160 days of life. If he has a week left of that clock and does something the Judge approves of he gets another 160 days. There are also rolls to prolong the current Sekhem level by a few days to a few months depending on the current level. The system is set up in such a way that ten dice of Sekhem are virtually impossible to get an extension on while 1 dot is almost guaranteed. There are penalties applied to each attempt to extend the duration beyond the first, though. So eventually your Sekhem rating will fall.<br /> <br /> It pisses off the Judges something fierce but you can also suck out the magic of a relic. You can drain up to the relic's rating in Sekhem and add those levels to your current score, maximum of ten. Judges and Arisen society appreciates this action about as well as vampires approve of a fledgling diablerizing an elder, though. So either keep your activities secret or be prepared to be shunned and/or attacked by rivals and Guilds who do not approve of this use of vessels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}